# Per-Dockerfile ignore for the `jvm` worker image (PRD #39 Decision 5). MIRRORED
# from templates/base/Dockerfile.dockerignore — keep in lockstep. BuildKit picks it
# up by the "<Dockerfile-name>.dockerignore" naming next to templates/jvm/Dockerfile;
# its patterns resolve relative to the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT (the repo root), not this
# directory. It must NOT exclude the source trees the chat agent reads (api/ web/
# agent/ docs/ specs/ prds/ e2e/ scripts/ *.md) — only secrets, VCS, submodules,
# deps, and build artifacts. See templates/base/Dockerfile.dockerignore for detail.

# Secrets — must NEVER enter the build context (`.env*` also catches `.envrc`).
.env*
**/.env*

# VCS + submodule metadata + the large inspiration/ submodules.
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
inspiration/

# Installed deps + build artifacts (regenerated; not source).
**/node_modules
web/node_modules
agent/node_modules
**/dist
web/dist
agent/dist
